  <h1>Own your AI chat data</h1>
    <p class="lead">AI chats are becoming a second brain. If that brain only exists inside someone else’s web app, you don’t own it — you’re renting access to your own words.</p>
    <h2>Three risks of “leaving it in the tab”</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Product risk</strong> — features, pricing, and UIs change</li>
      <li><strong>Account risk</strong> — lockouts, plan changes, lost access</li>
      <li><strong>Tool sprawl</strong> — ChatGPT + Claude + Perplexity + Gemini + Grok = fragmented memory</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What ownership looks like</h2>
    <p>Files on your disk. Open formats. Backups you control. That’s it. Not a new cloud silo with another password.</p>
    <h2>Where TotalRecalls fits</h2>
    <p><strong>TotalRecalls</strong> is a Windows app for exporting multi-assistant chat history into a local library. One-time <span data-tr-price>$24</span>. Built so we never need to collect your provider session tokens on a server.</p>
    <h2>A simple policy for yourself</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Export on a schedule (monthly) or after big projects</li>
      <li>Keep one parent folder, e.g. <code>AI-Archive</code></li>
      <li>Back up that folder like photos and tax docs</li>
    </ol>
